Now I understand the structure:

- File: `dir/{id}.note`, content is `id\n---\ntitle\n---\npinned_flag\n---\nbody`.

- `load_all` reads all files in the directory, splits on SEP with splitn(4), and takes
 id from parts[0] — meaning the id is inside the content, and the filename is derived
